 {label} applies. Which clue is the strongest indication?",options=sits,kind='standard')
    if variant==6:
        return dict(common,prompt=f"Which statement correctly describes {label}?",options=defs,kind='standard')
    return None

# Hand-authored nature-of-guiding-principles questions (criterion 2.1).
manual_21=[
("Which statement BEST describes how the ITIL guiding principles should be used?",["They should be considered together and adapted to the circumstances","Each principle belongs to one specific practice","They form a mandatory sequence that must be followed in order","An organization should select one principle and ignore the others"],"The guiding principles are universal recommendations that interact and should be applied together as relevant to the situation.","Gebruik de principes samen en pas ze toe op de situatie. Het zijn geen fasen, geen één-op-één koppeling aan practices en geen keuze voor slechts één principe.","Principles interact; they are not a sequence."),
("A team is working in unfamiliar circumstances. What is the BEST way to use the guiding principles?",["Use all relevant principles as guidance while adapting decisions to the context","Choose the principle that sounds most important and use only that one","Apply them as fixed procedures without considering the situation","Use them only after a service has already been designed"],"The principles guide decisions in many circumstances but do not replace judgement or context.","De principes geven richting in allerlei omstandigheden, maar zijn geen vaste procedures. Context en professioneel oordeel blijven nodig.","Guidance + context, not rigid rules."),
("Which statement about the scope of the guiding principles is CORRECT?",["They can guide organizations regardless of changes in goals, strategies or types of work","They apply only to service management improvement initiatives","They apply only to the six service value chain activities","They apply only when an organization adopts every ITIL practice"],"The principles are intended to guide an organization broadly, including when its objectives or circumstances change.","De principes zijn breed toepasbaar en niet beperkt tot één soort initiatief, value-chainactiviteit of volledige ITIL-adoptie.","Broadly applicable guidance."),
("Which is the MOST appropriate relationship between the guiding principles and organizational decisions?",["The principles influence decisions without dictating one mandatory action in every case","Each principle defines one compulsory process that must be implemented","The principles replace governance decisions when teams disagree","Only senior management should use the principles"],"Guiding principles inform and shape decisions; they are not rigid process instructions and are relevant across the organization.","Principes sturen het denken, maar schrijven niet voor elke situatie één verplichte actie voor. Ze zijn niet alleen voor management.","Guide decisions; do not dictate procedures."),
("Which TWO statements about the guiding principles are correct?\n1. They are recommendations that can guide an organization in all circumstances.\n2. They are used independently so that one principle does not affect another.\n3. They should be considered together when making decisions.\n4. They prescribe a fixed order for service management work.",["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"Statements 1 and 3 are correct. The principles are broadly applicable and interact; they are not independent stages or a fixed sequence.","1 en 3 zijn juist. Principes zijn breed toepasbaar en werken samen; ze zijn geen losse fasen en hebben geen vaste volgorde.","Broad guidance, used together."),
("Which statement is NOT consistent with the nature of the guiding principles?",["Each principle must be completed before the next principle is considered","Several principles may be relevant to the same decision","The principles can support decisions when circumstances change","The principles are intended as recommendations rather than rigid instructions"],"The principles are not sequential stages. Several can apply at once and they are used as recommendations.","De principes vormen geen stappenplan. Meerdere principes kunnen tegelijk relevant zijn en ze zijn bedoeld als aanbevelingen.","Not a sequence."),
("An organization changes its sourcing strategy and operating model. How should the guiding principles be treated?",["Continue using the relevant principles as guidance in the new circumstances","Replace them with a new set because they only apply to the old operating model","Use only 'think and work holistically' because sourcing has changed","Suspend them until all new processes are documented"],"The guiding principles remain applicable when strategies, goals or organizational structures change.","Ook bij een andere sourcingstrategie of organisatiestructuur blijven de relevante principes bruikbaar.","Principles survive changes in context."),
]
for i,(p,opts,en,nl,hook) in enumerate(manual_21):
    add(dict(id=qid('2.1'),criterion='2.1',lo=2,tag='Using guiding principles',prompt=p,options=opts,why=en,whyNl=nl,hook=hook,kind='list' if 'TWO' in p else ('negative' if 'NOT' in p else 'standard')))

# Hand-authored interconnected-value-chain questions (criterion 5.1).
manual_51=[
("Which statement BEST describes the service value chain?",["It is a flexible operating model whose activities can be combined in different ways to form value streams","It is a mandatory six-step lifecycle that every service must follow in the same order","It is a list of practices assigned one-to-one to six departments","It is the governance body that authorizes all service changes"],"The service value chain is a flexible operating model. Organizations combine its six activities in different patterns to create value streams.","De service value chain is flexibel. De zes activiteiten vormen geen vaste volgorde en practices zijn niet exclusief aan één activiteit gekoppeld.","Six activities; many possible value streams."),
("A team assumes every request must pass through all six value chain activities in the same order. Which correction is BEST?",["Value streams can combine value chain activities in different sequences and may repeat activities as needed","Every value stream must use all six activities exactly once","Only the Improve activity may be repeated","The order is fixed, but activities may be skipped"],"The chain is not a fixed lifecycle. A value stream uses activities as needed to respond to demand and facilitate value creation.","Een value stream gebruikt activiteiten naar behoefte; er is geen verplicht schema waarin alle zes precies één keer voorkomen.","Not a fixed pipeline."),
("What is the MAIN relationship between a value stream and the service value chain?",["A value stream is a specific combination of value chain activities used to create and deliver value","A value stream is another name for one value chain activity","The service value chain is created separatel